@startuml LaPrizzaDomainModel
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing true
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
hide methods

title Domain Model Excerpt - WEB03 Role-Based Navigation (User Aggregate)

' -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
' USER AGGREGATE.
' WEB03 introduces NO new domain concept: it only consumes the current roles
' and the active state of the User, resolved by the back end (AA03).
' -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
package "User Aggregate" <<Rectangle>> {

    class User <<entity>> <<aggregateRoot>> {
        + active : boolean
    }

    class UserId <<vo>> {
        + value : string
    }
    note right of UserId
        - UserId is a unique identifier for a user.
        - Example: "USR-00123".
        - The SPA never sends another user's id
          to obtain "own data" sections (AA05).
    end note

    class Email <<vo>> {
        + emailAddress : String
    }

    class UserName <<vo>> {
        + name : String
    }

    enum UserRole <<enum>> {
        ADMINISTRATOR
        MANAGER
        EMPLOYEE
        CUSTOMER
    }
    note right of UserRole
        Website roles (Table 1):
        - ADMINISTRATOR -> Administrator
        - MANAGER -> LaPrizza Manager
        - EMPLOYEE -> Restaurant Staff
        - CUSTOMER -> Customer
        Guest is NOT a role: it is the absence
        of an authenticated session and gives
        access only to the public sections.
    end note

    User "1" *-- "1" UserId : identified by >
    User "1" *-- "1" Email : has >
    User "1" *-- "1" UserName : has >
    User "1" --> "0..*" UserRole : assigned >

    note bottom of User
        <b>What WEB03 reads from this aggregate</b>
        (always through GET /api/v1/auth/me, never from the JWT)
        - roles: the set of sections shown in the menu is the UNION
          of the sections granted to each role (Table 1).
        - active: an inactive account, or an account with no role,
          sees only the public sections plus an access-denied message.
        <b>What WEB03 does NOT do</b>
        - It never changes roles or the active state (AA06 / AA07).
        - It never decides authorization on its own: hiding a menu
          option is always complemented by the back-end check
          (AuthMiddleware + RoleMiddleware) on every request (AA05).
        <b>Note</b>
        - "Navigation section" is a presentation concept of the SPA
          (frontend/src/navigation), not a domain concept, and is
          therefore not part of the domain model.
    end note
}

@enduml